<main class="site-doc" lang="en"><header><div class="wrap"><h1>Tutorials</h1><p>Create a page, add an event, and publish with eServer.</p></div></header><div class="wrap"><section><h2>Create your first page</h2><ol><li>In ePage Studio, open a project and create a page.</li><li>Add a panel, set its text and properties, and save the page.</li><li>Check that the page directory contains <code>page.xml</code> and appears in the project tree.</li></ol><p><a href="./features?v=guide#main-interface">See the Studio workspace</a></p></section><section><h2>Add a click event</h2><ol><li>Select a button or panel on the canvas.</li><li>Open its <code>onClick</code> event and add a JavaScript handler.</li><li>Publish and click the control in a browser to verify the result.</li></ol><pre>sender.style.backgroundColor = "#46368b";</pre><p><a href="./samples#layers">Try a view-switching example</a></p></section><section><h2>Publish with eServer</h2><ol><li>Register your project directory in the eServer project list.</li><li>Set the domain and default page where appropriate.</li><li>Open your public page URL. Test links and image responses in addition to the HTML.</li></ol><p>For example, the page directory <code>features</code> in this project is available at <code>/ePage.dev/features</code>.</p></section></div></main>`;
